# Finding: RBQA-AI39-F002
# Byte-at-a-time HTTP header reader persists in remote peer HTTPS ingress

triage:RBQA-AI39-F002
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "RBQA-AI39-F002" ;
  triage:title "Byte-at-a-time HTTP header reader persists in remote peer HTTPS ingress" ;
  triage:description "The byte-at-a-time HTTP header/body reader (read_http_headers in crates/atm-core/src/api.rs:570) was built to retire for local transports in AI.39 with HttpFrameReader (buffered, chunk-based delimiter search via memchr), but still runs in production for remote peer HTTPS ingress via route_peer_http_request in crates/atm-daemon/src/https_transport.rs:609. This duplicates the exact decision logic now owned by HttpFrameReader: delimiter search, content-length parsing, header/body size-cap enforcement. AI.39's non-goals correctly defer read_http_response and 'HTTPS call sites' to AI.43, but AI.43's scope is explicitly limited to response framing (read_http_response) only and never mentions read_http_request or route_peer_http_request. This leaves the remote, untrusted-peer request-parsing path on a permanent one-byte-syscall loop with no sprint currently scheduled to close it, and no mechanical lint prevents this pattern from persisting or reappearing in a production network path." ;
  triage:category "scope_gap" ;
  triage:severity "important" ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-AI" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:repeatable true ;
  triage:sweepScope "workspace" ;
  triage:status "open" ;
  triage:dispatchReady false ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-07-31T17:30:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:highestOpenBranch triage:s39-occurrence ;
  triage:rootCause "Scope gap: AI.39 introduces HttpFrameReader for local transports but excludes HTTPS call sites. AI.43 explicitly limits scope to response framing only, leaving request-path uncovered. No mechanical boundary enforcement prevents byte-at-a-time parsing from persisting in remote ingress." ;
  triage:dispatchNotes "This is a cross-sprint scope gap requiring plan-level coordination. May need: (1) routing to AI.43 sprint-doc to extend scope to read_http_request, (2) a dedicated follow-up sprint for remote HTTPS request framing, (3) or explicit decision to defer past phase-AI." ;
  triage:occurrences triage:s39-occurrence, triage:integrate-occurrence .

